        "name": "missingValues",
        "optional": true,
        "defaultValue": "None",
        "description": "Fill character used to represent missing values. To activate a non-default setting, set the `useMissCharAsDefaultForFill` property to `true`, and use one of the following values to `missingValues`:\n\n* `none` (for the reader) or `NONE` (for the writer): Treats all data as values.\n* `spaces` (for the reader) or `SPACES` (for the writer): Interprets a field consisting of only spaces as a missing value. Default for flat file and fixed-width formats.\n* `zeroes` (for the reader) or `ZEROES` (for the writer): Interprets numeric fields consisting of only `0` characters _and_ character fields consisting of only spaces as missing values.\n* `nulls` (for the reader) or `NULLS` (for the writer): Interprets a field consisting only of `0` bytes as a missing value. Default for COBOL copybook schema.",
        "possibleValues": [
          "none",
          "spaces",
          "zeroes",
          "nulls"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "segmentIdent",
        "optional": true,
        "defaultValue": "None",
        "description": "Segment identifier in the schema for fixed-width or COBOL copybook schemas. Required when parsing a single segment or record definition if the schema includes multiple segment definitions.",
        "possibleValues": [
          
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "recordParsing",
        "optional": true,
        "defaultValue": "strict",
        "description": "Specifies the expected type of separation between lines or records:\n\n* `strict`: Line break is expected at exact end of each record. `strict` is the default.\n* `lenient`: Line break is used, but records can be shorter or longer than the schema specifies. Don't use `lenient` if your payload lacks line breaks. The other options to `recordParsing` support records that lack line breaks.\n* `noTerminator`: Records follow one another with no separation. This option is preferred for fixed-length records that lack a line break.\n* `singleRecord`: The entire input is a single record.\n\nNote that schemas with type `Binary` or `Packed` don't allow for line break detection, so setting `recordParsing` to `lenient` only allows long records to be handled, not short ones. These schemas also currently only work with certain single-byte character encodings (so not with UTF-8 or any multibyte format).",
        "possibleValues": [
          "strict",
          "lenient",
          "noTerminator",
          "singleRecord"
        ]
      },
      {
